  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.models.CatalogItem\": {\n        \"summary\": \"A data model class representing a catalog item in an ordering system. The class encapsulates catalog item information including SKU number, description, price, inventory count, and lead time. It provides three constructors: a default no-args constructor, a parameterized constructor accepting all fields, and a copy constructor for creating a duplicate CatalogItem. Key methods include standard getters and setters for all five fields (skuNumber, description, price, inventory, leadTime), and a validate() method that validates the SKU number and description fields using the Utility class helper methods. The validate() method returns a JSON-formatted string containing errors if validation fails, or null if the item is valid. This is a typical POJO (Plain Old Java Object) following the JavaBean pattern, suitable for use in data transfer, persistence, or business logic operations within the ordering system.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/models/CatalogItem.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
